FONTS

Literata is not mine and is not covered by either licence above. It is bundled
under the SIL Open Font License 1.1, whose full text is in
`licenses/Literata-OFL.txt` and must travel with any copy of these files:

  app/src/main/res/font/literata_regular.ttf
  app/src/main/res/font/literata_italic.ttf
  app/src/main/res/font/literata_bold.ttf
  app/src/main/res/font/literata_bold_italic.ttf

  SPDX-License-Identifier: OFL-1.1
  Copyright 2017 The Literata Project Authors
  <https://github.com/googlefonts/literata>

These four files are modified versions of the upstream release, and the OFL
requires saying so. Upstream ships two variable fonts, roman and italic, with
an optical-size and a weight axis. Each of the four here is a static instance
cut from those at `opsz` 12 — the axis default, and the value drawn for running
text — and at `wght` 400 or 700, then subset to Latin: Basic, Supplement,
Extended-A and Extended-B, general punctuation, currency, and the f-ligatures.

That is 466 KB for four faces where the two variable fonts alone are 1.8 MB.
The cost is that Literata's Greek and Cyrillic are gone; a note written in
either renders in the system font instead, because Android falls back per
glyph. Deliberate, and reversible by re-cutting from upstream.

The OFL permits this. Its restriction is on names, and Literata declares no
Reserved Font Name, so the modified files may keep the name they came with.


